@title Motor at variable frequency: curves, readouts, model label, and the project without a motor
@area Simulate
@sizes 1366x768
# The golden motor starter project has a motor: Simulate > Motor at variable frequency shows the
# curves (each labelled with its frequency, rated and continuous lines labelled), the readout
# table, the model label and the folded list of what the model leaves out.
open crates/novo-tests/tests/golden/v0.1-motor-starter.novo
wait 20
key ctrl+k
wait 3
text Motor at variable frequency
wait 4
key Enter
wait 30
expect "What this model leaves out"
expect "rated torque"
expect "Breakdown"
shot motor-curves
click_text "What this model leaves out"
wait 10
shot leaves-out-open
scroll 330 400 -800
wait 10
shot leaves-out-scrolled
click_text "What this model leaves out"
wait 10
scroll 330 400 -800
wait 10
shot leaves-out-unfolded
check_layout
# A project without a motor says so.
key Escape
wait 5
key ctrl+n
wait 20
key ctrl+k
wait 3
text Motor at variable frequency
wait 4
key Enter
wait 20
expect "no motor"
shot no-motor
